WEBVTT

1
00:02.450 --> 00:05.750
Introducing the Workbench for Grok Build.

2
00:05.750 --> 00:08.250
We love Grok. We love Linux.

3
00:08.250 --> 00:10.550
We just don't love living in the terminal.

4
00:10.550 --> 00:13.350
So we built a window onto Grok Build

5
00:13.350 --> 00:17.150
for vibe coders that would prefer a visual representation

6
00:17.150 --> 00:19.550
to staring at lines in the terminal.

7
00:19.550 --> 00:21.350
Here's what that looks like.

8
00:21.350 --> 00:24.550
The Workbench for Grok Build keeps it pretty simple.

9
00:24.550 --> 00:25.550
Here's the deal.

10
00:25.550 --> 00:28.150
You tell the agent what you want in natural language

11
00:28.150 --> 00:29.750
and press send.

12
00:29.750 --> 00:31.150
It starts thinking.

13
00:31.150 --> 00:32.950
Before it changes any files,

14
00:32.950 --> 00:34.950
it'll stop and ask for your permission

15
00:34.950 --> 00:37.950
and you can approve either for this one action

16
00:37.950 --> 00:39.950
or for the whole session.

17
00:39.950 --> 00:41.250
And at the end of the turn,

18
00:41.250 --> 00:42.750
it'll give you a little note at the bottom

19
00:42.750 --> 00:44.550
and tell you what it costs.

20
00:44.550 --> 00:47.550
Another feature of the bench is it allows you to review

21
00:47.550 --> 00:50.750
and undo the agent's changes one at a time.

22
00:50.750 --> 00:52.550
Your own edits are never touched,

23
00:52.550 --> 00:54.850
so your work stays secure.

24
00:54.850 --> 00:58.350
Here, the agent just made three changes.

25
00:58.350 --> 00:59.650
This drawer on the right

26
00:59.850 --> 01:02.550
will list every file it touched with the real count

27
01:02.550 --> 01:04.650
of the lines added and removed.

28
01:04.650 --> 01:07.450
You can open one and see it before and after,

29
01:07.450 --> 01:08.650
side by side.

30
01:08.650 --> 01:11.250
If you don't like this change, just click undo.

31
01:11.250 --> 01:13.850
It'll tell you in plain words what that will do

32
01:13.850 --> 01:16.850
and you confirm it and that one change is gone.

33
01:16.850 --> 01:18.750
The other two will stay put.

34
01:18.750 --> 01:20.250
Here's the part that matters most.

35
01:20.250 --> 01:22.050
If you've edited the file yourself,

36
01:22.050 --> 01:24.850
undoing the agent's work never touches what you wrote,

37
01:24.850 --> 01:27.250
so your work stays secure.

38
01:27.250 --> 01:29.750
A context meter in the upper right-hand corner

39
01:29.750 --> 01:32.550
shows how full the agent's working memory is

40
01:32.550 --> 01:34.250
at any given time.

41
01:34.250 --> 01:36.750
The numbers actually add up because we checked

42
01:36.750 --> 01:38.350
and as they get crowded,

43
01:38.350 --> 01:40.750
you can click compact to clear up space

44
01:40.750 --> 01:43.050
and see that real number drop.

45
01:43.050 --> 01:45.350
Below that, the privacy panel

46
01:45.350 --> 01:48.350
shows each setting next to its source

47
01:48.350 --> 01:50.450
and the one that matters that shares your data

48
01:50.450 --> 01:56.000
is clearly visible and asks for your permission first.

49
01:56.100 --> 01:59.800
Now watch us interrupt the agent mid-sentence on purpose.

50
01:59.800 --> 02:02.500
There's no blank screen, no fake, everything's fine.

51
02:02.500 --> 02:06.300
Instead, a plain red line tells you exactly what happened.

52
02:06.300 --> 02:08.100
The agent was interrupted.

53
02:08.100 --> 02:10.000
Then the app reloads every session

54
02:10.000 --> 02:12.600
from the file saved on your machine.

55
02:12.600 --> 02:15.800
Marks it recovered and the next question answers fine,

56
02:15.800 --> 02:16.800
still here.

57
02:16.800 --> 02:19.000
So if the agent dies, you get the truth

58
02:19.000 --> 02:20.700
and it comes back.

59
02:20.700 --> 02:26.630
Never a blank screen or a fake, everything's fine.

60
02:26.630 --> 02:29.430
The Workbench keeps everything in one place.

61
02:29.430 --> 02:33.930
You can easily rename things, run several at once.

62
02:33.930 --> 02:37.130
Every session on your machine is in one list,

63
02:37.130 --> 02:43.920
group by folder.

64
02:43.920 --> 02:46.820
So that's the Workbench for Grok Build.

65
02:46.820 --> 02:49.220
It doesn't change what Grok can do.

66
02:49.220 --> 02:53.620
It makes what it already does easy to see and easy to use.

67
02:53.620 --> 02:56.820
Browse for a file instead of typing out the path,

68
02:56.820 --> 02:59.520
start a session and find it again later,

69
02:59.520 --> 03:02.220
rename your work, undo any changes,

70
03:02.220 --> 03:05.320
and always know where your privacy settings stand.

71
03:05.320 --> 03:07.720
The Workbench runs on your own machine,

72
03:07.720 --> 03:12.020
it collects nothing itself, and it's free and open source.

73
03:12.020 --> 03:15.020
We made Grok Build easier to build with.

74
03:15.020 --> 03:17.020
That's the Workbench for Grok Build.
